    "title": "Nate Schatzline posts on rallies and political advocacy in Texas",
    "text": "Nate Schatzline, a Republican member of the Texas State House representing District 93 since 2023, has recently posted several statements on his social media account addressing political and religious topics.\nOn November 11, 2025, Schatzline wrote, “Fact Check: True It’s all Jihad.”\nThe following day, November 12, 2025, he posted about his involvement in rallies and events focused on mobilizing faith communities. Schatzline stated, “Rally/Event #25 (I think ) over the last 6 weeks in this new full time role mobilizing the Church to TAKE BACK AMERICA with the National Faith Advisory Board & @FLJ_Official Tonight I’m speaking in Abilene with @tpusafaith & @TPUSA ACU Chapter as well as pastors from across”.\nLater that same day, he congratulated an associate with the message: “HUGE! Congrats my friend! Time to save Texas!”\nSchatzline assumed office in the Texas State House after being elected in 2023, succeeding Matt Krause as representative for District 93.",
